## Exclude content from a prefetch

Optimizing a prefetch also means excluding content from it. Some subtrees are expensive enough to produce that you would rather not pay for them on every prefetch of the route.

Awaiting [`navigation()`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/navigation) above the work leaves it out of every prefetch, so it is produced on the navigation. The nearest [`<Suspense>`](https://react.dev/reference/react/Suspense) fallback is what the user sees while it streams in. Take the dashboard again, where a ranking keyed on the session is too expensive to produce for every link into the route:

```tsx filename="app/dashboard/recommendations.tsx" highlight={6}
import { cookies } from 'next/headers'
import { navigation } from 'next/cache'

async function Recommendations() {
  const session = (await cookies()).get('session')?.value
  await navigation()
  const items = await rank(session)
  return <List items={items} />
}

async function rank(session?: string) {
  'use cache: private'
  return db.recommendations.rank({ session })
}
```

The session is read above `navigation()`, so it resolves in the shell like any other session data. Only the ranking is left out, and it keeps its cache lifetime.

Without it, keeping a subtree out of a prefetch means leaving it uncached, which gives up that lifetime on the navigation too. Awaiting `navigation()` inside a cached scope is not allowed, so put the caching directive on a function called below it, as `rank` does here.

For a subtree that would otherwise sit in the App Shell, but that a `<Link prefetch={true}>` should still resolve before the click, use [`prefetch()`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/prefetch) instead.

Unlike [`connection()`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/connection), `navigation()` does not make the subtree request-dependent. This lets reusable content keep its cache lifetime while waiting for navigation. See [How `navigation()` differs from `connection()`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/navigation#how-navigation-differs-from-connection) for the full comparison.

## Test prefetched and deferred content

